TODO: REPLACE THIS PLACEHOLDER WITH THE REAL MEDIAPIPE MODEL

This directory should contain the file `selfie_segmenter.tflite` (~250 KB, float16)
which is loaded by `expo.modules.callkit.video.BackgroundProcessor` at runtime to
perform real per-pixel person segmentation for the video-call background blur /
virtual-background feature (Wave 17 gap F3).

DOWNLOAD URL (Google AI Hub — public, Apache 2):
  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/image_segmenter/selfie_segmenter/float16/latest/selfie_segmenter.tflite

INSTALL STEP (one-time per clone, must be done manually — cannot be automated
via package.json or gradle because we don't want to fetch a 250 KB binary on
every npm install):

  curl -L -o modules/expo-callkit/android/src/main/assets/selfie_segmenter.tflite \
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/image_segmenter/selfie_segmenter/float16/latest/selfie_segmenter.tflite

  # Then DELETE this .TODO file:
  rm modules/expo-callkit/android/src/main/assets/selfie_segmenter.tflite.TODO

After this, rebuild the Android app (scripts/ship.sh android "msg"). Without
this asset, BackgroundProcessor.ensureSegmenter() logs the failure and falls
back to a full-frame blur — UI still works but person is not kept sharp.

The same model is also needed on iOS — see TODO at top of
modules/expo-callkit/ios/BackgroundProcessor.swift for the Xcode steps.
